<task id="061" project="email-communication-intelligence-r2">
  <metadata>
    <title>ReconciliationWorkspace composition + apply UX A4/A5/A6 to ReconciliationBrowseShell — wire grid → shell(renderTabs) → reconcile tabs</title>
    <phase>5 Pillar E — Reconciliation UI (mount build)</phase>
    <gate>startable — deps 050–058 complete (grid + shell + tabs exist + exported)</gate>
    <status>not-started</status>
    <rigor>FULL</rigor>
    <rigor-reason>Modifies .tsx in the shared lib (new composition + shell layout changes); "implement/create component"; wires gate + citation across components.</rigor-reason>
    <model-tier>sonnet</model-tier>
    <model-tier-reason>Additive composition + a bounded layout change to an existing shell, with a complete spec (prototype App.tsx + UX doc + the shell's own renderTabs contract as explicit references); no architectural novelty or security surface.</model-tier-reason>
    <effort>high</effort>
    <parallel-group>none</parallel-group>
    <parallel-safe>false</parallel-safe>
    <parallel-reason>Shared lib @spaarke/communication-components (also edits the 053 shell); /conflict-check before PR (contended with r5).</parallel-reason>
    <deps>050,051,052,053,054,055,056,057</deps>
    <tags>react, typescript, frontend, fluent-ui</tags>
    <estimated-effort>3-5 hours</estimated-effort>
  </metadata>

  <prompt>
    Build a new presentational `ReconciliationWorkspace` in @spaarke/communication-components that renders the EXISTING
    `ReconciliationGrid` and, on row-open, the EXISTING `ReconciliationBrowseShell` (the task-053 SprkModal + "N of M"
    two-pane shell) — feeding its `renderTabs` slot a TabList → Related-to (052) / FieldUpdateReconcileTab (055) /
    TaskReconcileTab (056). ALSO apply the owner UX layout items to the shell's two-pane body: A4 larger modal size,
    A5 thin scrollbars, A6 50/50 split with a manual horizontal drag-resize (PanelSplitter). Compose + enhance the
    shipped components — do NOT re-implement the grid, shell, reader, or tabs; do NOT introduce a BrowseModal wrapper
    (the shell already IS the modal).
  </prompt>
  <role>SPAARKE platform developer. Expert in React + Fluent UI v9 + the Spaarke shared component libraries. Follow ADRs strictly; compose + enhance, do not fork.</role>
  <goal>
    (1) `ReconciliationWorkspace` is exported from @spaarke/communication-components: renders ReconciliationGrid, opens
    ReconciliationBrowseShell on row-open with the queue + initialIndex, and supplies `renderTabs` = Related-to / Fields /
    Tasks (mounting the 052/055/056 tabs) with the NFR-10 gate + citation wiring. (2) ReconciliationBrowseShell's
    two-pane body honors A4 (SprkModal size xl/full), A5 (thin scroll via ModalScrollArea), and A6 (PanelSplitter 50/50,
    drag-resizable). Package build + jest green.
  </goal>

  <context>
    <background>
      Tasks 050–058 built + exported the grid, the SprkModal-based `ReconciliationBrowseShell` (with a `renderTabs` right
      slot already designed for the 052/055/056 tabs), and the reconcile tabs — but nothing composes them into a mounted
      surface, and the shell's two-pane body predates the owner's A4/A5/A6 layout requirements. The prototype's mock
      App.tsx is the UX reference. This task creates the production composition + applies A4/A5/A6 so task 062 can mount
      ONE component in two hosts.
    </background>
    <relevant-files>
