  <justification>
    <existing>No component composes grid + shell + tabs; the shell EXISTS with a `renderTabs` slot but nothing supplies the tabs or the grid→shell wiring. Closest neighbor is the prototype mock App.tsx (not production). `grep -rln ReconciliationGrid src/solutions` → zero external mounts.</existing>
    <extension>The shell (053) is extended for A4/A5/A6 (in-place layout change — no new component). The grid→shell→tabs orchestration is genuinely new glue that no existing single component provides; hence a new ReconciliationWorkspace, not an extension of any one component.</extension>
    <cost-of-doing-nothing>Without it, each host (code page + SpaarkeAi widget, task 062) must independently wire the grid to the shell + supply renderTabs + the gate + citation state — guaranteed drift between the two surfaces and doubled test surface. And without A4/A5/A6 on the shell, the owner-approved layout requirements ship unmet.</cost-of-doing-nothing>
  </justification>

  <constraints>
    <constraint source="project">SCOPE: compose + enhance EXISTING components. Do NOT re-implement ReconciliationGrid, ReconciliationBrowseShell, its reader, or the reconcile tabs. Do NOT add a BrowseModal wrapper — ReconciliationBrowseShell already is the SprkModal-based shell (A1 satisfied; see its types header + notes/053).</constraint>
    <constraint source="ADR-050">SCOPE: A4 larger modal. Bump the ReconciliationBrowseShell SprkModal size to "xl" (or "full") per docs/standards/MODAL-DESIGN-SYSTEM.md sizes.ts — more real estate for the email + attachment reader.</constraint>
    <constraint source="project">SCOPE: A6 50/50 drag-resize. Replace the shell's fixed two-pane grid with a `PanelSplitter` defaulting to 50/50 with manual horizontal drag-resize (reader | renderTabs). SCOPE: A5 thin scroll — wrap the reader + tab-slot scroll regions in ModalScrollArea (the shared thin-scroll convention).</constraint>
    <constraint source="ADR-021">SCOPE: styling. Fluent v9 semantic tokens only; light/dark; no hard-coded colors.</constraint>
    <constraint source="ADR-012">SCOPE: shared lib. ReconciliationWorkspace is context-agnostic — accept IDataverseClient + authenticatedFetch + theme (+ uiScale) via props; no host coupling, no direct Xrm.</constraint>
    <constraint source="project">SCOPE: behavior. NFR-10 — the Fields/Tasks tabs in renderTabs are gated until a Related-to record is confirmed; re-scope on override. NFR-11 — use the shell's existing reader + activeCitation (task 054); no second reader/citation mechanism. Apply-routing per the UX doc §C (Accept→apply{overrideValue}, Reject→dismiss, task edited-identity→ad-hoc+dismiss, +New→ad-hoc) is already inside the tabs — wire their callbacks through.</constraint>
  </constraints>

