      <pattern name="prototype-composition" location="spaarke-prototype/projects/email-communication-intelligence-r2-uat/src/App.tsx">The UX-reference orchestration (grid overrides, browse open, 50/50 split, tabs, save/undo, gate) to mirror with production components + real data.</pattern>
      <pattern name="PanelSplitter" location="src/client/shared/Spaarke.UI.Components/src/components/PanelSplitter/PanelSplitter.tsx">The 50/50 drag-resize splitter (A6) for the shell's two-pane body.</pattern>
    </patterns>
  </knowledge>

  <steps mode="directional">
    <step order="0">Load this POML + the UX doc + notes/053. Read ReconciliationBrowseShell.tsx/.types.ts (renderTabs, queue, initialIndex, activeCitation, uiScale), ReconciliationGrid (onRecordOpen, membershipResolver), the two tab contracts, PanelSplitter, ModalScrollArea, sizes.ts. Confirm the tabs mount cleanly into renderTabs + the grid onRecordOpen supplies the row. If a contract does not compose, FIRE the escalation trigger.</step>
    <step order="1">Apply A4/A5/A6 to ReconciliationBrowseShell.tsx: SprkModal size → xl/full (A4); two-pane body → PanelSplitter 50/50 drag-resize (A6); reader + tab-slot scroll regions → ModalScrollArea thin scroll (A5). Keep the shell's existing reader, nav, citation, and renderTabs contract intact.</step>
    <step order="2">Create ReconciliationWorkspace.tsx: render ReconciliationGrid (configId, dataverseClient, membershipResolver, authenticatedFetch, theme). onRecordOpen(row) → build the queue (from grid data) + initialIndex → open ReconciliationBrowseShell.</step>
    <step order="3">Supply the shell's renderTabs = a TabList → Related-to (052) / Fields (FieldUpdateReconcileTab, 055) / Tasks (TaskReconcileTab, 056), passing regarding/onProposalResolved/onCitationClick. Wire the NFR-10 gate (Fields/Tasks disabled until Related-to confirmed; re-scope on override) and citation click → the shell's activeCitation.</step>
    <step order="4">Export ReconciliationWorkspace from the component barrel (components/index.ts).</step>
    <step order="5">Write RTL tests: grid renders; row-open opens the shell; splitter present at 50/50; gate blocks Fields/Tasks until Related-to confirmed; citation click sets activeCitation; a Fields Accept calls the apply path. Reuse existing test mocks (authenticatedFetch mock, injected client, FluentProvider wrapper). Add/adjust ReconciliationBrowseShell tests for the A4/A5/A6 layout changes.</step>
    <step order="6">Run the package build + jest; fix to green.</step>
    <step order="7">Update TASK-INDEX.md: set 061 status to ✅.</step>
    <step order="8">Document the composition + the shell A4/A5/A6 change in projects/email-communication-intelligence-r2/notes/.</step>
  </steps>

  <escalation>
    <trigger>If a production component's contract does NOT compose as expected (e.g., the reconcile tabs cannot mount into the shell's renderTabs slot, a tab's regarding/onProposalResolved contract is incompatible, or PanelSplitter cannot replace the shell's two-pane grid without breaking the reader/nav), STOP and escalate per CLAUDE.md §6 — do NOT fork or re-implement a component to force the composition.</trigger>
  </escalation>

  <tools>
    <tool name="npm">Build + test the shared lib (jest).</tool>
  </tools>

