  </outputs>

  <acceptance-criteria>
    <criterion testable="true">ReconciliationWorkspace is exported from @spaarke/communication-components and renders ReconciliationGrid given configId + dataverseClient.</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">Opening a grid row opens ReconciliationBrowseShell (SprkModal, NOT a new BrowseModal) at size xl/full, with its renderTabs slot mounting a TabList → Related-to / Fields / Tasks.</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">The shell's two-pane body uses a PanelSplitter defaulting to 50/50 with a working drag handle; reader + tab scroll regions use the thin-scroll convention.</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">NFR-10: Fields/Tasks tabs are gated until a Related-to record is confirmed; re-scope on override.</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">A Fields "Accept" invokes the apply path with the (possibly overridden) value; a citation click sets the shell's activeCitation and the reader jumps/highlights.</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">Negative: ReconciliationWorkspace takes IDataverseClient + authenticatedFetch via props and does NOT reference Xrm directly (ADR-012); no grid/shell/reader/tab code is re-implemented.</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">Package build succeeds and all jest tests pass (incl. updated ReconciliationBrowseShell layout tests).</criterion>
  </acceptance-criteria>

  <notes>
    ReconciliationBrowseShell already IS the modal + reader + renderTabs slot (task 053, SprkModal + nav; its types header explicitly documents the renderTabs right-pane for 052/055/056/057). So 061 is mostly wiring (grid→shell, tabs→renderTabs, gate + citation) plus a bounded in-place layout change to the shell for A4/A5/A6. The prototype App.tsx is the interaction reference; production swaps its raw Dialog/mock-reader/local-decisions for the shell + real tabs + real apply endpoints (already deployed).
  </notes>

